cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "Kimodo is NVIDIA's. The code and the weights are licensed separately -- cite both."
title: "Kimodo: a kinematic motion diffusion model for humanoid motion generation"
type: software
authors:
  - name: "NVIDIA Toronto AI Lab"
repository-code: "https://github.com/nv-tlabs/kimodo"
license: Apache-2.0
references:
  - type: software
    title: "Kimodo-SOMA-SEED-v1.1 and Kimodo-SOMA-RP-v1.1 checkpoints"
    authors:
      - name: "NVIDIA"
    url: "https://huggingface.co/nvidia/Kimodo-SOMA-SEED-v1.1"
    notes: "NVIDIA Open Model License, not Apache-2.0."
  - type: software
    title: "SOMA-X skeleton"
    authors:
      - name: "NVlabs"
    repository-code: "https://github.com/NVlabs/SOMA-X"
notes: "THE APACHE-2.0 BADGE COVERS THE CODE AND NOT THE WEIGHTS. Kimodo-SOMA-* and
  Kimodo-G1-* are under the NVIDIA Open Model License, which permits commercial use and
  is the shippable variant. Kimodo-SMPLX-RP-v1 carries the more restrictive NVIDIA
  Internal Scientific Research and Development License, and it is also a SMPL-X
  checkpoint, which is blocklisted here -- motion travels SOMA-X to ANNY, so that
  variant is off the route twice over and is not a constraint on this row.
  weftspun/interactor-kimodo-text-to-motion is an HTTP wrapper that raises
  NotImplementedError outside stub mode and holds no model."
